Z||000000||Drapes85Fiero||06-15-2000||06:10 PM||||  Hey I need to find the P/N's for the Front Lower ball joints for an 85 Fiero and also the rear ball joints.  I have a 1600 mile trip to Lincoln Ne coming up in 2 weeks and I need to replace them before I go any help would be great.  Oh yea also where can I get them cause GM no longer makes them or the front rack.  Thanks once again!!! <BR>  Dave<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||06-15-2000||07:25 PM||||You can't go wrong if you buy Moog brand ball joints and tie rod ends. All the major auto parts stores around here can order those parts and have them in within 1 to 2 days. I know because I bought all new ball joints that way. Make sure to get the slotted (adjustable) upper ball joints, if you ever need them. I sometimes look up part numbers at wrenchhead.com or carparts.com||||reg||1
Z||000002||Zman302||06-16-2000||12:57 AM||||Heres the part #'s you need....<BR>Moog parts<BR>front k6273<BR>rear  K6257<P>I found these at carparts.com but you should be able to find these localy.  I know i can get them next day in TRW and if you have a Auto Value store in your area like the ones in my area they usually have them in one of there warehouses and can have them that afternoon.   Happy hunting<BR>||||reg||1
